developer: <permissions instructions> Filesystem sandboxing defines which files can be read or written. `sandbox_mode` is `workspace-write`: The sandbox permits reading files, and editing files in `cwd` and `writable_roots`. Editing files in other directories requires approval. Network access is restricted. Approval policy is currently never. Do not provide the `sandbox_permissions` for any reason, commands will be rejected. The writable roots are `/tmp`, `/workspace`. </permissions instructions>
